  "body": "## What changed\n- A 2D pocket that cuts as Zigzag now closes with one ring on each boundary loop of the cutter-center area. Auto resolves to Zigzag, so Auto gets the rings too. The rings cut the outer wall and each island wall.\n- The pocket uses the existing rest-pocket plan (`pocket_zigzag::rest_passes`). The rows stand 0.01 mm inside the area, and the rings follow the area boundary.\n- The row points now stand on the 1 um lattice.\n- A Zigzag pocket with blended turns now holds its blends to the crossing law (`hold_crossings`), as the rest pocket does. A fillet that would cross a ring stays a sharp turn.\n\n## Cause\n- `pocket_over_with_relief` used the rows-only plan for an ordinary Zigzag pocket. Only rest pockets got the closing rings.\n- The rows touch a side wall or an island only at their ends. A cusp stays between each two ends over the full depth.\n- With a 6 mm tool and a 2 mm stepover, the cusp is 0.17 mm on a straight wall and 0.75 mm on an R4 corner. Verify has no law for that material, so the program passed as clean.\n- Two more problems came from the change itself:\n  - The 0.01 mm gap puts the row ends off the lattice. A helix entry snaps its turns to the lattice. Two levels' helices at one off-lattice start then differed by 3.5e-7 mm, and the post check read them as crossings (`setup_align`). Lattice row points remove this.\n  - Blended row turns crossed the new rings (`app corner_blend`). The crossing hold removes this.\n\n## Tests\nNew pins: `crates/motion/tests/pocket_wall_finish.rs`. The pocket is 60 x 40, with R4 corners and a 16 mm island. The tool is 6 mm, with a 2 mm stepover.\n- `auto_pocket_with_island_finishes_walls_and_island`\n- `zigzag_pocket_with_island_finishes_walls_conventional`\n- `zigzag_pocket_without_island_finishes_walls`\n- `blended_zigzag_pocket_finishes_walls_without_crossings`\n- `blended_zigzag_turns_do_not_cross_the_closing_rings`\n\nThe first four tests measure the scallop on each wall at the floor. The limit is 0.02 mm. They also check `verify::crossed_pairs`.\n\nRed before the fix: the first four tests fail on unchanged code (outer wall scallop 0.755 mm; 0.919 mm when blended).\n\nMutation checks:\n1. Old `pocket.rs` guard: the 4 wall pins go red. Restored: green.\n2. No lattice snap in `rest_passes`: `setup_align::the_pocket_and_face_kinds_cut_the_flipped_part_and_post` goes red (\"post blocked - 4 warning(s): ... cross in XY at shared depth\"). Restored: green.\n3. No crossing hold for Zigzag: `blended_zigzag_turns_do_not_cross_the_closing_rings` goes red (12 crossing pairs, the same pairs as `app corner_blend`). Restored: green.\n\nGate:\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` on head 6e3e4397b: 678 steps, 0 failed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\nExpected-change test: `setup_align` asserted the island clearance with a square box (`max(|x|, |y|) < 21.9`). A closing ring at a rounded corner is legal but failed that check. The assertion now measures the Euclidean distance to the 40 x 40 block (at least 1.9 mm for the 4 mm tool).\n\n## Goldens moved\nThere are 18 changed files, all for one pocket case and the two first-part sample programs:\n- `crates/app/tests/golden/pocket_zigzag_plate_with_island.cl` and `pocket_zigzag_plate_with_island_blended.cl`.\n- `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/*/pocket_zigzag_plate_with_island.nc`: 12 dialects, plus the Tormach `explain_` file.\n- `examples/first-part.nc` and `examples/catalog/2d/first-part/first-part.nc`. The 2D Pocket1 of that part is Auto.\n\nIn each NC file, only motion blocks change: the rows move 0.01 mm inward, and the ring blocks are new. Block numbers after them move by the same count. No header, tool, spindle or coolant line changes. The `.camproj` files do not change.\n\n## Not exercised\n- The QA project from the report (`q01-first-post.camproj` on skull). The motion pin rebuilds the same shape.\n- `pocket_avoid` (Do not touch) and the 3D pocket levels still cut Zigzag rows with no ring. #3129 tracks them.\n- A pre-existing defect: in a narrow band, two helix entries of different passes can overlap. The post check blocks it. That is before and after this change. #3129 notes it.\n- Heavy lanes (`cargo xtask gate heavy`) were not run.\n\n## Overlaps\n- #2842 touches `crates/motion/src/machining2d/pocket_emit.rs` (the level ladder line). This PR does not change that file.\n\nChangelog: 2D Pocket with strategy Zigzag or Auto now finishes the pocket walls and islands with a closing pass, so no wall scallops stay above the stock to leave.\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #3021\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
